{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792334275,"nonce":"/F9uAlBRfqTirzaRnLiLOIZpdNc=","title":"Settings page: build, libraries, terminal, color scheme, key bindings, extensions","message":"The user asked for a workspace preferences page that covers more than the build file: terminal, build, haxelibs, extensions, color scheme and key bindings. It replaces the separate Build and Terminal tabs with one Settings tab: a list of sections down the left and the section chosen beside it, as VS Code's Settings editor.\n\nBuilt:\n- Store: `.rayde/settings.json`, a section per area (`terminal`, `appearance`); saving a section keeps the others. The terminal's own `terminal.json` is gone.\n- Build: the existing hxml form, with the library section moved out.\n- Libraries: haxelib's libraries, a click puts one in or out of the build's -lib, Add installs one haxelib lacks, each installed library can be updated or removed. haxelib runs as a background job (LibraryManager); `RAYDE_HAXELIB` names a stand-in for tests. Jobs have no input, so a prompt gets end of file; install and update pass --always.\n- Terminal: the existing form.\n- Color scheme: system, light or dark, and one of ashui's three bundles from a picture of each; applied at once (ThemeState, and the window's own appearance), written to the file, applied at launch from Main.\n- Key bindings: one command list drives the command center, the page and key dispatch. Chord model (`mod+shift+p`, `ctrl+``, `f5`), one key per command, user changes in `.rayde/keybindings.json`, a recorder (click a key or the pencil), conflicts marked, reset one or all. A key typed alone is refused: it would run a command while typing.\n- Extensions: lists folders with an extension.json under `.rayde/extensions` here or in the home folder; nothing runs them (see 971d58e).\n- Opens from the gear, Cmd+, the build file in the Explorer, and the command center (Open Settings, Manage Libraries, Color Scheme, Open Keyboard Shortcuts, Show Extensions). `RAYDE_SETTINGS=\u003csection\u003e` opens it at launch.\n- Checks for chords, bindings, store, appearance, haxelib parsing and a job against a stand-in, extension discovery. Snapshots of every section in both themes, driving the page as the pointer and keyboard would, with haxelib and the home folder stood in.\n\nChecked in a live window: starting on Hybrid light, and on system (dark here), come up as asked. Choosing a scheme with a click in a live window was not driven (clicks cannot be synthesised there); it is covered offscreen.\n\nOpen:\n- A search over all settings, as VS Code has. The sections are forms, not a registry; 971d58e makes settings a registry that extensions contribute to, which is when search can cover everything.\n- User settings beside workspace settings (~/.rayde).\n- Editor settings: tab size, insert spaces, font size, word wrap, line numbers, the minimap when ashui has it.\n- Key bindings: chord sequences (cmd+k cmd+s), `when` clauses, several keys on one command, keys that depend on the keyboard layout (symbols are read as on a US keyboard) and Option-letter chords on a Mac (the key typed is the composed character, not the physical key).\n- Terminal: a font size; keys the terminal keeps for the program while it has focus are still the old rule (Command and Ctrl+`).\n- Color scheme: an accent colour, custom themes, light and dark chosen separately by time of day.\n- Libraries: search haxelib online, install from git or a local folder, choose a version, `haxelib dev`.\n- Extensions: enabling and disabling, capabilities, errors; waits on 971d58e.","files":null}]}